# openssl/libssl3: unbounded memory growth in QUIC server listener
# (CVE-2026-14456, HIGH).  Added 2026-08-18 after CI #501/#502/#504
# (Build & Push Trivy gate).  NO fixed version exists in ANY Debian
# release as of 2026-08-18 (bookworm & bookworm-security 3.0.20-1~deb12u2
# vulnerable, trixie postponed, sid unfixed per security-tracker), so
# there is nothing to upgrade to; the app does not use QUIC server
# listeners.  Re-review at expiry; when bookworm ships a fixed openssl,
# DELETE this entry and let the gate enforce the upgrade.
# expiry="2026-12-31"
CVE-2026-14456

# ── wget (added 2026-08-16, issue #233 healthcheck hardening) ─────────
# wget was added to the production image (issue #233): Coolify's own
# healthcheck probe injects `wget` when Coolify manages the healthcheck
# (custom_healthcheck_found=false), and the curl-only image made every
# probe fail with "wget: not found" (rc 1) → rollback of every deploy.
# The wget advisories below are HIGH findings present in the bookworm
# package (1.21.3-1+deb12u1) with NO fixed version available upstream yet
# (FixedVersion=N/A in the OSV/Trivy DB as of 2026-08-16).  The image only
# runs wget as a localhost healthcheck probe (unauthenticated DoS /
# user-interaction vectors are not reachable from outside the container),
# so these are accepted risk in the same category as the curl entries
# above.  Re-review at expiry; if a fixed wget lands in bookworm, remove.
# expiry="2026-12-31"
CVE-2026-58469
# wget: unauthenticated availability DoS via crafted response (no fix yet)
# expiry="2026-12-31"
CVE-2026-58471
# wget: unauthenticated availability DoS via crafted response (no fix yet)
# expiry="2026-12-31"
CVE-2026-58472
